# Keep secrets and local state OUT of the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in the builder stage, so anything not
# excluded here is baked into an image layer — .env carries the plaintext
# DATABASE_URL password, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the
# image. Runtime config arrives via docker compose `environment:`, never by
# reading a file inside the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build + dependency artifacts — rebuilt inside the image anyway,
# and copying them in busts the layer cache on every change.
node_modules
.next
out
dist

# VCS + editor noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local data volume (mounted at runtime, must not be pre-seeded)
data

# Docs that don't belong in a runtime image
docs
README.md
CLAUDE.md
DESIGN.md
